A constant-speed stage traces a **rectangle**: area $=$ speed $\times$ time.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,3.2);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.4,0);
\fill[blue!12] (0,0)--(0,2.3)--(3.6,2.3)--(3.6,0)--cycle;
\draw[thick,blue] (0,2.3)--(3.6,2.3);
\node[font=\small] at (1.8,1.15) {Rectangle};
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-0.5,1.6) {Speed};
\node[font=\small] at (2.2,-0.55) {Time};
\node[font=\small] at (2.2,-1.25) {Constant speed};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A constant acceleration or deceleration starting or ending at rest traces a **triangle**: area $=\dfrac{1}{2}\times\text{base}\times\text{height}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,3.2);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.4,0);
\fill[blue!12] (0,0)--(3.6,2.7)--(3.6,0)--cycle;
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0)--(3.6,2.7);
\node[font=\small] at (2.4,0.8) {Triangle};
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-0.5,1.6) {Speed};
\node[font=\small] at (2.2,-0.55) {Time};
\node[font=\small] at (2.2,-1.25) {Starts or ends at rest};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A stage where the speed changes between two non-zero values traces a **trapezium**.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,3.2);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.4,0);
\fill[blue!12] (0,0)--(0,1.1)--(3.6,2.7)--(3.6,0)--cycle;
\draw[thick,blue] (0,1.1)--(3.6,2.7);
\draw[dashed] (0,1.1)--(3.6,1.1);
\node[font=\small] at (1.8,0.55) {Rectangle};
\node[font=\small] at (2.65,1.55) {Triangle};
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-0.5,1.6) {Speed};
\node[font=\small] at (2.2,-0.55) {Time};
\node[font=\small] at (2.2,-1.25) {Speed changing between two values};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

