The cruising stage lasts $12-5=7$ seconds; braking lasts $18-12=6$ seconds.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.3cm,y=0.22cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(20,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,21);
\draw[thick,graphRed] (0,0)--(5,18)--(12,18)--(18,0);
\draw[dashed,black] (5,0)--(5,18);
\draw[dashed,black] (12,0)--(12,18);
\path (3.3,5) node {$A$};
\path (8.5,9) node {$B$};
\path (14,5) node {$C$};
\foreach \x in {0,5,12,18} {\path (\x,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};}
\path (0,18) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$18$};
\path (9,-3.2) node {Time (s)};
\path (-3,10) node[rotate=90] {Speed (m/s)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$A$ and $C$ are triangles; $B$ is a rectangle.

$\begin{aligned}d&=A+B+C\\&=\frac12\times5\times18+7\times18+\frac12\times6\times18\\&=45+126+54\\&=225\text{ m}\end{aligned}$

